# Deliberately suppressed checks (rationale in GUIDANCE.md, "Static analysis" section):
#  - readability-braces-around-statements: this codebase uses single-line
#    guard clauses ("if (!x) return unexpected(err);") pervasively for the
#    std::expected-based early-return style; this mirrors GCC/Linux kernel
#    style (both cited as explicit style inspirations) and is not a
#    correctness risk for single-statement, no-nested-if guard clauses.
#  - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: fires on mathematically
#    commutative arguments (mulmod(a,b,m), gcd(a,b)) where "swapping" is
#    not a bug, and on small internal-linkage helpers with a single,
#    already-tested call site.
#  - readability-convert-member-functions-to-static: verifier classes
#    (KurepaVerifier, ToyMod7Verifier, PigeonholeVerifier) are deliberately
#    modeled as stateful objects (a natural extension point for future
#    configuration such as brute-force limits or audit logging), even
#    though no instance currently holds state.
#  - readability-function-cognitive-complexity: threshold raised, not
#    disabled, for the DPLL unit-propagation loop; it is a single,
#    well-tested hot function where splitting it further reduces rather
#    than improves auditability.
Checks: >
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  bugprone-*,
  readability-*,
  cert-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -readability-convert-member-functions-to-static
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: 'math-hunter/(include|src)/.*'
CheckOptions:
  - key: readability-function-cognitive-complexity.Threshold
    value: '40'
